J. SELECTION-BIAS DIAGNOSTIC (held-out-action filter)
  [PASS] share of candidate training states dropped for naming a held-out answer  989 dropped vs 6000 kept (14.2%)
      Held-out answers are 246/2315 = 10.6% of the answer list, and a
      pair exposes two actions, so if both were answers the expected
      drop rate would be 1-(1-0.106)^2 = 20.1%. Not every action is an
      answer, so anything between ~10% and ~20% is the filter doing
      its job.
      The stronger argument is structural: the held-out set is chosen
      by sha256(salt|answer), which is independent of every game
      property, so the filter cannot preferentially remove hard or
      easy states — only a pseudorandom 10.6% of words.

